FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: convert_safe
Signature: int convert_safe(char inf[], char *output, size_t output_size)
Description: /**
 * @brief Convert infix expression to postfix notation with bounds checking.
 *
 * Safely converts an infix expression to postfix by validating the output buffer
 * and ensuring the result fits within the provided size. Resets the internal
 * operator stack before each conversion.
 *
 * @param inf Null-terminated infix expression string to convert.
 * @param output Buffer to store the resulting postfix expression.
 * @param output_size Size of the output buffer in bytes.
 *
 * @return 0 on successful conversion, -1 if output is NULL, output_size is too
 *         small, or the converted result would overflow the buffer.
 *
 * @note This function calls initStack() to reset internal state before conversion.
 * @note The output buffer must be at least 25 bytes to be considered valid.
 */

Dependencies: convert, initStack

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION (REFERENCE ONLY - do NOT copy into test):
```c
